WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.240
Buddhists teach anatta: there
is no fixed, lasting self.

2
00:00:05.290 --> 00:00:10.390
Yet the Buddha rejected the view that all
we experience is caused by past karma.

3
00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:13.910
And there is no single
Pali word for conscience.

4
00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:17.720
So if there is no fixed self, who is free?

5
00:00:17.770 --> 00:00:19.120
Who is to blame?

6
00:00:19.170 --> 00:00:21.720
And who listens to conscience?

7
00:00:21.770 --> 00:00:26.000
In this mission, you'll place Buddhist
teaching on a line from hard determinism

8
00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:27.780
to libertarianism.

9
00:00:27.830 --> 00:00:30.960
Then you'll meet a king's
questions about a mango thief,

10
00:00:31.010 --> 00:00:33.320
and a red-hot iron ball.

11
00:00:33.370 --> 00:00:37.030
Your mission: find out who
is free, who is to blame,

12
00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:40.910
and who listens to conscience,
if there is no fixed self.
